{
	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "g-23cae583fd75c7",
			"x": 720,
			"y": 0,
			"width": 1200,
			"height": 189,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Event Model\nThe kernel's event model from K1 (#18, PR #36).\n\nColours: purple = types, orange = header and Reading, red = open or flagged, none = Decisions.\n\nRendered 2026-11-22 by agent:claude-opus-5-5",
			"color": "2"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-f9bdf542b054fa",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Event envelope",
			"x": 720,
			"y": 309,
			"width": 440,
			"height": 796
		},
		{
			"id": "g-fbe3e03f52accb",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 379,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 266,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Event** *(record)*\n```\nid        sha256:<hex>\ncauses    sorted set of EventId\nrecorded  Hlc time\noccurred? ms\nsalt      32 hex\nbody      Body\n```\nThe constructor recomputes the id and refuses a mismatch.",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-9e9a17c2a8b852",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 685,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 146,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Body** *(sealed)*\nWhat happened: one kind of event.\nOnly kind so far: `AcceptedAction`. More kinds are added here.",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-d1b416be4bb0b5",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 871,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**AcceptedAction** `{ by, action }`\n**By** `{ principal, on_behalf_of?, grant, via }`, plain names for now.\n**Action** `{ definition: Identity, args: Json }`. The definition says vocabulary and version.",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-62f96fbf3d6b97",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Assertions",
			"x": 1280,
			"y": 309,
			"width": 440,
			"height": 982
		},
		{
			"id": "g-94403005fbbc15",
			"x": 1320,
			"y": 379,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 218,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Assertion** `(identity?, attribute?, value?)`\nAn assert action carries one or more tuples, appended together.\nTuple *n* of event *e* is `e/n`.\nAny mix of present and absent parts is accepted; meaning is left open.",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-b106636ef9b68b",
			"x": 1320,
			"y": 637,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 146,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Value** *(sealed)*\n`Literal` (string or integer): `{\"literal\": …}`\n`Ref` (an Identity): `{\"ref\": …}`",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-0eb2db8a230325",
			"x": 1320,
			"y": 823,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Examples**\n```\nx/0 = (,,)                entity\nx/1 = (x/0, name, \"Kitchen\")\ny/0 = (anna, owns, ref x/0)\ny/1 = (y/0, since, 2024)\nz/0 = (x/1, retracted, \"true\")\n```"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-96ad7d10d3ab80",
			"x": 1320,
			"y": 1057,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Identity** `sha256:<hex>` or `sha256:<hex>/<n>`\nTuples, attributes, definitions.\n**Basic**: well-known identities `assert`, `retracted`, `label` (hashes of `khora/basic/<name>`).",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-0620ad13ac5dc1",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Ids and time",
			"x": 720,
			"y": 1411,
			"width": 440,
			"height": 676
		},
		{
			"id": "g-f277affcc23a84",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 1481,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 170,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**EventId** `sha256:` + SHA-256 of the event's canonical JSON without `id`.\nThe salt stops guessing content from the id; the hash keeps integrity and commits to history.",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-54d44d21565b2b",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 1691,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 170,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Json** (canonical, RFC 8785 subset)\nObjects, arrays, strings, 64-bit integers. Sorted keys, no whitespace.\nRefuses lone surrogates, nesting deeper than 1000. Own code, no dependencies.",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-9d719d3fe25c07",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 1901,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 146,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Hlc** hybrid logical clock\nms << 16 | counter in one long. `next(after)` is later than `after` and than every earlier result. Refuses past `Long.MAX_VALUE`.",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-b4358a63c45322",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Event graph and frontiers",
			"x": 1280,
			"y": 1411,
			"width": 440,
			"height": 676
		},
		{
			"id": "g-4b7312238598e6",
			"x": 1320,
			"y": 1481,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 170,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**EventGraph** in memory (stand-in until K2)\n`append` returns `Appended` or `Refused`: `MISSING_CAUSE`, `NOT_AFTER_CAUSES`, `DUPLICATE`.\nEvents without causes are roots.",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-5662f815088466",
			"x": 1320,
			"y": 1691,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 122,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Frontier** `{ heads }`: the heads and everything that caused them.\n`Frontier.of(ids, source)` reduces to heads.",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-c98400d1877d54",
			"x": 1320,
			"y": 1853,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 194,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**FrontierCheck**\n`validate`: `Valid` or `Invalid(missing)`, which refuses a frontier lacking a cause.\n`compare`: BEFORE, AFTER, EQUAL, CONCURRENT.\n`combine`: heads of the union.\nIterative walks.",
			"color": "6"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-411c155cb6606e",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Decisions (Issue #18 run)",
			"x": 720,
			"y": 2207,
			"width": 840,
			"height": 676
		},
		{
			"id": "g-533a898ae41fdb",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 2277,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 170,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[An accepted action is one kind of event]]**\n*design · active*\nSupersedes [[An event is an accepted action, and an assert is the basic action]]."
		},
		{
			"id": "g-1d4f031a1fa928",
			"x": 1160,
			"y": 2277,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 122,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Assertions are tuples with identity]]**\n*design · active*\n`(,,)` instantiates an entity."
		},
		{
			"id": "g-c7f1e3a8119e81",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 2487,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 122,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[An event carries several assertions]]**\n*design · active*\nIdentified by `<event id>/<index>`."
		},
		{
			"id": "g-2b441e8b0741c5",
			"x": 1160,
			"y": 2487,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 170,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Event ids are salted hashes of canonical JSON]]**\n*design · active*\nKept for integrity and history, for interoperability."
		},
		{
			"id": "g-2216eff4c331d7",
			"x": 760,
			"y": 2697,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 122,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[An assert's id is the identity of what it asserts]]**\n*design · active*"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-2cda1b0c2c1d78",
			"x": 1160,
			"y": 2697,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 146,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Events are the basic unit of khora]]**\n*design · from the Issue #21 run*\nFrontiers are sets of events closed under causes."
		},
		{
			"id": "g-c33964c4314ac4",
			"x": 1680,
			"y": 2207,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 242,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Reading · 2026-11-22**\n- Built and tested: 80 tests, PR #36 (draft, stacked on #35).\n- Nothing reads assertions yet; the tuple model pays off from K6 and B2.\n- Event kinds beyond accepted actions: not decided.\n- A genesis event per log: not decided.",
			"color": "2"
		},
		{
			"id": "g-8203949e9e7e79",
			"x": 1680,
			"y": 2489,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 362,
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Open or flagged**\n- Task 6: replace K4's `EventId` and `Frontier` placeholders, after the Issue #21 run closes.\n- Security: `By` names are unauthenticated; the salt is in plain text.\n- Performance: `compare` walks whole histories; `EventGraph` has one lock.\n- Change later: attribute definitions (cardinality, type); atomic multi-event writes (K3).\n- Deferred minors: see the ledger and PR #36.",
			"color": "1"
		},
		{
			"id": "spec",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 0,
			"width": 560,
			"height": 525,
			"color": "6",
			"text": "## Spec · Event Model\n\n**Purpose:** show the kernel's event model as built in [[Issue #18 Event types ids and clock]] (K1): the event envelope, assertions, ids, the clock, the event graph and frontiers.\n\n**Show:** each kernel type with its fields and rules; the Decisions it rests on; what is open or deferred.\n\n**Context:** the run's Design section, its Decisions, and `src/kernel/src/main/java/khora/kernel/event` and `json`.\n\n**Judgement:** show what the code does today, not the ADRs. Mark provisional parts.\n\n**Layout:** row 1 the envelope and assertions; row 2 ids, clock, graph and frontiers; row 3 Decisions and the Reading.\n\n**Triggers:** re-render when the event package or the run's Decisions change.\n\n*Draft spec by agent:claude-opus-5-5, to be agreed with a team member.*"
		}
	],
